# Path to the KB-Manager knowledge base repository
KB_MANAGER_DIR=/path/to/KB-Manager
DATA_DIR=/path/to/data

# API keys
GEMINI_API_KEY=...
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# Preferred, and preferred by the code rather than by convention: settings.py:17
# and cli_tools/_common/openrouter.py read it, and all three external.py checks
# (gemini, gpt, discuss) route THROUGH OpenRouter when it is set and fall back to
# the direct provider key only when it is not (_external/gemini.py:77,
# cross.py:77, discuss.py:28). With neither set the caller refuses before
# openrouter.py is ever reached, printing "OPENROUTER_API_KEY or
# GEMINI_API_KEY not set".
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is deliberately not listed. settings.py:14 still defines it,
# but no module imports it -- the three external tools import only
# GEMINI/OPENAI/OPENROUTER. Setting it configures nothing, and a key in this
# file that nothing reads invites the belief that a Claude-side check is wired
# up. (NLPROVER_VERIFIER_CMD='claude -p ...' shells out to the Claude CLI, which
# uses its own credentials, not this variable.)

# Polite-pool identity for the OpenAlex API. Read by
# cli_tools/_search/citation_graph.py:104 and cli_tools/_workspace/refs_bib.py:45,
# both defaulting to "". Unset, requests leave the OpenAlex polite pool and are
# rate-limited harder, so `search citation-graph` and `workspace refs-bib` get
# slower and flakier rather than failing outright.
OPENALEX_MAILTO=you@example.org

# The problem workspace the Claude Code dispatch hook writes into. Read only by
# .claude/hooks/dispatch_log.py:246; it is the first and only resolution step
# that cannot be wrong. The fallback -- cwd or an ancestor containing STATUS.md
# -- cannot fire in the normal layout, because workspaces live under DATA_DIR in
# a different repository than the one Claude Code is launched from. Unset, the
# hook resolves nothing and writes nothing, silently. Measured: 159 rows across
# 6 workspace dispatch.jsonl files, zero carrying source: "hook" -- every row
# was written by hand. platform_mix, prompt_shape and token_cost in `gate speed`
# are unmeasured until this is exported. See README "Claude Code orchestrator
# startup".
NLPROVER_WORKSPACE=/path/to/data/workspace/<problem>

# Cold-start verifier command for `verify.py dispatch --run`; the dispatch text
# is fed on stdin. Read at cli_tools/verify.py:202. Unset, --run refuses and
# says so (verify.py:209) rather than silently doing nothing -- a verification
# that did not happen must not look like one that passed. Without --run,
# verify.py prints the dispatch text and this is not needed.
# Left commented on purpose. `.env` is loaded by settings.py, so an uncommented
# value here ships as a live default -- `--run` would then quietly execute
# whatever `claude` is on PATH instead of refusing, which is the opposite of
# what every surrounding rule promises. Uncomment the line you mean.
# NLPROVER_VERIFIER_CMD=claude -p --permission-mode acceptEdits
# NLPROVER_VERIFIER_CMD=codex exec
